learn=[('Pass credentials through the right channel', 'The external stdio process receives a classroom API key through env. HTTP MCP servers receive an Authorization header. Keys remain on the backend and are redacted from the configuration viewer.'), ('Expand project placeholders at runtime', 'The project experiment writes ${DEMO_MCP_TOKEN} into .mcp.json, then supplies that variable through the runtime environment. Both stdio env and HTTP headers authenticate without putting the generated credential in the file.'), ('Keep OAuth in your application', 'The classroom provider performs a real local authorization-code flow with consent, state validation and S256 PKCE. The app exchanges the code and hands the token to the SDK. This is a local teaching provider, not GitHub OAuth or a production identity service.'), ('Use GitHub with read-only scope', 'The GitHub example uses your locally configured PAT to connect to the real remote MCP server. It exposes only list_issues, restricts the query to three public issues and records actual connected status and completion.'), ('Detect unavailable servers', 'Keep initialization separate from current status. Treat failed and needs-auth as unavailable; pending alone is not failure. The bad-token experiment keeps a valid server usable while the invalid-credential server supplies no data.'), ('Reconnect after fixing the cause', 'The recovery experiment starts with a controlled HTTP outage, records the unavailable state, restores the service and invokes reconnectMcpServer on the same running query. It then requests real data on a second turn.')]
document('/','MCP auth. <em>Detect and recover.</em>','Credential channels, app-side OAuth, real GitHub and observable recovery.','<div class="flow"><div><b>01 · Authenticate</b><p>env, headers and app-side OAuth</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>02 · Detect</b><p>Actual current server status</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>03 · Recover</b><p>Fix the cause, reconnect and verify</p></div></div><section class="panel" id="controls"><h2>Explore MCP authentication and recovery</h2><p id="configuration" class="meta">Checking local server…</p><label for="mode">Authentication experiment</label><select id="mode"><option value="stdio-env">stdio · credential supplied through env</option><option value="http-header">HTTP · bearer header authentication</option><option value="json-expansion">Project config · ${VAR} expansion</option><option value="oauth-handoff">OAuth · local consent and PKCE handoff</option><option value="bad-token-health">Bad token · detect and continue with healthy server</option><option value="reconnect">Recover · restore service and reconnect</option><option value="github">GitHub · read three public issues</option></select><button id="run" class="primary" disabled>Run authentication experiment →</button><p class="meta">Local labs use fresh generated classroom credentials. GitHub uses GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN from your private .env. No credential is printed. In OAuth mode, approve the clearly labelled local classroom consent below.</p></section><section class="step" id="oauth-panel" hidden><h2>Application-owned classroom OAuth consent</h2><iframe id="oauth-frame" title="Local classroom OAuth provider" style="width:100%;height:320px;border:1px solid #d4e5fa;border-radius:16px"></iframe><p>This is a local teaching provider. The application validates state and PKCE, exchanges the code and retains the access token on the server. The Agent SDK does not run this browser flow.</p></section><div class="workspace"><section class="panel" id="outcome"><h2 id="status" aria-live="polite">Ready</h2><p>Latest SDK-reported cost: <strong id="cost">—</strong></p><p class="meta">Session: <span id="session">—</span></p><div id="answer" class="markdown-body"></div><p id="notice" class="note"></p></section><section class="panel" id="option-panel"><h2>Options actually passed · secrets omitted</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="options" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Compare credential delivery, project settings and approved names. Actual header and env values are used internally but are not included in this projection.</p></section></div><section class="step" id="configuration-panel"><h2>Actual configuration · credential values redacted</h2><label for="configuration-file">Generated configuration</label><select id="configuration-file"></select><pre class="json-view"><code id="configuration-content" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Project mode shows literal variable placeholders. Other modes redact generated or real credential values before displaying configuration. Neither real .env nor raw credentials are served.</p></section><section class="step" id="discovery-panel"><h2>Actual initialization snapshot</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="discovery" class="language-json">{}</code></pre></section><section class="step" id="connection-panel"><h2>Actual current connection snapshots</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="connections" class="language-json">[]</code></pre><p>The host polls mcpServerStatus for up to twelve seconds when pending. The record preserves before and after-reconnect snapshots separately. It does not relabel the initial state.</p></section><section class="step" id="recovery-panel"><h2>Actual reconnection acknowledgement</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="recovery" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Recovery restores an intentional local outage, then invokes the SDK reconnect control. It does not claim to refresh a third-party token or reproduce a particular automatic retry count.</p></section><section class="step" id="native-panel"><h2>Actual SDK tool-result projection</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="native" class="language-json">[]</code></pre></section><section class="step" id="evidence-panel"><h2>Verify authentication, status and real completion</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="evidence" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Local trace events record only successful or rejected authentication, HTTP status, consent validation and completion. GitHub output comes from the live read-only MCP call. No token values appear here.</p></section><section class="step" id="init-panel"><h2>Actual system/init projection</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="init" class="language-json">{}</code></pre></section><section class="step" id="run-history"><h2>Compare this browser’s experiments</h2><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Completed tools</th><th>Query results</th><th>Reconnect invoked</th><th>Latest servers</th></tr></thead><tbody id="history"></tbody></table></div><button id="download">Download redacted observations</button></section><section class="step" id="event-panel"><h2>Actual SDK messages</h2><ol id="events"></ol></section>','<script type="module" src="/client.js"></script>')
document('/learn.html','What you <em>will learn.</em>','Authenticate deliberately and distinguish server failure from query failure.',cards(learn))
env='GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN=your_read_only_token\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_api_key\nCLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6\nPORT=3125\n# Optional on Windows: CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH=C:/Program Files/Git/bin/bash.exe'
runsteps=[('Prepare the runtime', 'Use Node.js 24 or later and a funded model API account. Windows may need Git Bash. The six local labs generate their own short-lived classroom credentials. Only the GitHub mode needs a separate real token.', 'node --version\nnpm --version'), ('Install and create your .env file', 'From presentations, install dependencies and preserve an existing .env. Enter your keys locally. Shell values take precedence over the optional startup env file.', 'cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson25-mcp-auth-errors\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env'), ('Start the web application', 'Open the printed URL and keep the terminal running. The app starts its own local teaching services and the SDK starts the stdio process. No separate production provider is needed for the local labs.', 'npm start\n# http://127.0.0.1:3125'), ('Compare env, headers and project placeholders', 'Run the first three modes. Inspect redacted configuration and successful authenticated tool results. Project config contains placeholders while the runtime supplies a generated value.', 'npm run sample:env -- stdio-env\nnpm run sample:env -- http-header\nnpm run sample:env -- json-expansion'), ('Complete the classroom OAuth flow in the browser', 'Choose OAuth mode in the web app, click Run, then Approve classroom access in the embedded consent screen. The real local code exchange validates state and PKCE before the SDK connects. The CLI also emits the local consent URL; open it in your browser to approve.', 'npm run sample:env -- oauth-handoff'), ('Detect failure, recover and read GitHub issues', 'Run bad-token health and reconnect, then GitHub with your local PAT. GitHub is limited to list_issues for three public anthropics/claude-code issues. No writes or comments are allowed.', 'npm run sample:env -- bad-token-health\nnpm run sample:env -- reconnect\nnpm run sample:env -- github\nnpm test')]
body=''
for i,(title,explanation,code) in enumerate(runsteps,1):body+=f'<section class="step" id="run-step-{i}"><span class="number">{i:02}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{explanation}</p>'+snippet(code,'powershell')+'</section>'
body+='<section class="step"><h2>Your .env configuration</h2>'+snippet(env,'dotenv')+'<p>Keep the actual key private. No Managed Agents agent ID or environment ID is required. No duplicate snapshot is included.</p></section><section class="note"><h3>Troubleshooting</h3><p>Use the URL printed by startup. If another app occupies the port, change PORT and restart. If API credit is unavailable, add credit to the account used by this key. Authentication and connection failures remain visible; no saved data replaces a failed call. Approve classroom OAuth in the browser when that mode is selected. GitHub requires GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN and internet access.</p></section>'
body+='<section class="step" id="github-token"><h2>Configure GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN</h2><ol><li>Open <a href="https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new">GitHub’s fine-grained token page</a>.</li><li>Name the token, choose an expiration and select Public repositories (read-only).</li><li>Generate the token and save it locally as GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN in .env.</li><li>Restart the application. Keep the token out of chat and screenshots.</li></ol><p>This example reads public issues from anthropics/claude-code and needs no private-repository or write permissions.</p></section>'
document('/run.html','Configure and <em>run the app.</em>','Configure model and GitHub keys, then run the local and remote labs.',body)
specs=[('Validate the classroom task', 'src/config.ts', 'return { mode:', 'Accept one fixed mode. Browser input does not supply arbitrary endpoints, commands, tokens or GitHub repositories.', 0, 1), ('Supply the stdio credential', 'src/config.ts', 'CLASSROOM_API_KEY: lab.token,', 'The actual classroom credential is passed through the stdio server environment. The process authenticates to its local API; real model and GitHub keys are blanked for that child.', 1, 4), ('Set an HTTP bearer header', 'src/config.ts', 'headers: { Authorization:', 'HTTP servers receive a bearer header. Only redacted configuration is displayed, while the real value is used internally for the connection.', 1, 4), ('Write placeholder configuration', 'src/config.ts', 'env: { ...stdio.env, CLASSROOM_API_KEY: "${DEMO_MCP_TOKEN}" },', 'The project file stores a placeholder in stdio env and HTTP headers. The SDK runtime receives the actual value through its environment, so the file contains no generated credential.', 1, 3), ('Complete application-side OAuth', 'src/auth-lab.ts', 'trace.push({ event: "state_validated" });', 'The application validates state and exchanges the authorization code using its private PKCE verifier. This local teaching flow completes before the SDK receives the access token.', 1, 2), ('Load project settings and runtime env', 'src/agent.ts', 'DEMO_MCP_TOKEN: lab.token,', 'Supply the runtime variable used by the generated project configuration. Other experiments pass credentials directly through server config. These values stay outside the displayed projection.', 1, 3), ('Run the real SDK query', 'src/agent.ts', 'const run = query(', 'Streaming input keeps recovery on one running Query. Normal experiments use one turn; the reconnection experiment performs a health-check turn before requesting data.', 1, 3), ('Preserve initial status', 'src/agent.ts', 'initServers = message.mcp_servers.map', 'The initialization snapshot may differ from current connection state. Preserve it instead of assuming configured servers are usable or treating pending as permanent failure.', 3, 1), ('Poll current server status', 'src/agent.ts', 'const current = async', 'Inspect mcpServerStatus and record separate phase snapshots. Failed and needs-auth indicate an unavailable server; pending is polled rather than immediately treated as failure.', 1, 3), ('Fix the cause and reconnect', 'src/agent.ts', 'await run.reconnectMcpServer("secure-api");', 'The local outage is restored before the actual SDK reconnect control is invoked. Verify connected status and a completed tool call on the next turn of the same query.', 1, 3), ('Limit GitHub to read-only issues', 'src/config.ts', '"X-MCP-Tools": "list_issues",', 'The real GitHub connection uses the configured PAT, a read-only server header and only list_issues. A host guard additionally fixes the public repository and three-issue request.', 1, 4), ('Redact credentials before display', 'src/agent.ts', 'export function redactor', 'Remove actual configured and generated secrets, plus common token patterns, before rendering configuration or model text. The private .env remains excluded from Git and HTTP routing.', 1, 0), ('Render answers beside evidence', 'src/client.ts', 'if (e.type === "answer")', 'Sanitize and format actual Markdown. Keep it beside redacted authentication traces, server snapshots, reconnect acknowledgement and real tool results.', 1, 0)]
steps=[];arrows=[];lanes=['Student UI','App backend','OAuth provider','Agent SDK','MCP service']
for n,(title,source,anchor,explanation,a,b) in enumerate(specs,1):
 text=(APP/source).read_text(encoding='utf-8');lines=text.splitlines();idx=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if anchor in l)
 count={1:3,2:5,3:3,4:4,5:6,6:3,7:3,8:5,9:6,10:4,11:4,12:6,13:3}.get(n,1);code='\n'.join(lines[idx:idx+count]).strip()
 steps.append(dict(number=n,title=title,source=source,code=code,language='typescript',explanation=explanation,firstLine=idx+1,lastLine=idx+count,anchors=[lines[idx].strip()],sourceSHA256=hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest(),narration=f'Step {n}. {explanation} This source excerpt shows the corresponding application statement.'))
 arrows.append([a,b,f'{n}. {title}'])
(APP/'scripts/architecture-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(lanes=lanes,arrows=arrows,steps=steps),indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
